From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/pci-host: Add the Broadcom STB PCIe root complex

The BCM2712 (Raspberry Pi 5) has three PCIe root complexes of the kind
Linux's pcie-brcmstb driver serves ("brcm,bcm2712-pcie"): one for the
board's external connector, one for its RP1 I/O chip and one unused.
Each has a root port whose configuration space sits at the start of the
register window, an indexed window onto the other buses' configuration
spaces, up to four outbound windows from an aperture of CPU addresses
into PCI memory, up to ten inbound windows from PCI addresses onto the
system bus, an MSI target that raises its own level-2 interrupt
controller, and the link and reset controls the driver drives.

Add a model of it. The root port has the capabilities lspci shows on a
BCM2712 C1: power management, a PCI Express root port with no slot,
AER, virtual channel, a vendor-specific block, secondary PCIe and,
where the "l1ss" property asks, L1 PM substates. Its link has
"num-lanes" lanes at up to "max-link-speed", and "aspm-l0s" adds ASPM
L0s to L1. The private registers Linux writes to set the class code
and the link capabilities show in the configuration space.

The link trains at once while PERST# is deasserted, the root port's
bridge is out of reset, the PHY is powered and a device is on the
secondary bus. An empty port stays down, as the driver expects of a
connector with nothing in it. Asserting PERST# resets the secondary
bus; the "bridge-reset" GPIO input, or the RGR1 bit that the driver
uses without a reset controller, resets the root port, its command
register included. Configuration
reads and writes while the link is down, and accesses outside every
window, fail as the error-reporting controls ask: a bus error, or data
of all ones or of 0xdeadbeef.

The outbound windows map PCI memory into an aperture given by
"outbound-base" and "outbound-size", and the inbound windows map PCI
addresses onto "dma-memory", which devices use through the root bus's
IOMMU address space. The MSI target decodes writes whose data matches
the driver's pattern into one of 32 vectors. INTA to INTD and the two
level-2 controllers' outputs are the model's six interrupt outputs.
MISC_REVISION reads as "hw-revision".

With "preinit", a reset leaves the root complex as the boot firmware
leaves one it keeps trained for the OS: PERST# released, outbound
window 0 mapping the aperture's last 4 GiB to PCI 0, inbound RC_BAR2
mapping PCI 0x10_0000_0000 onto "dma-memory" from 0, 64 GiB, and the
root port forwarding memory to bus 1. The OS may use the link as it is
or reset the bridge and start over, as Linux does.
---
 hw/pci-host/Kconfig      | 7 +++++++
 hw/pci-host/meson.build  | 1 +
 hw/pci-host/trace-events | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/pci-host/Kconfig b/hw/pci-host/Kconfig
index bda6e16..461b041 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/pci-host/Kconfig
@@ -51,6 +51,13 @@ config PCI_EXPRESS_ASPEED
     select PCI_EXPRESS
     select PCIE_PORT
 
+config PCI_EXPRESS_BRCMSTB
+    bool
+    select PCI_EXPRESS
+    select PCIE_PORT
+    select BRCMSTB_L2_INTC
+    select MSI_NONBROKEN
+
 config PCI_EXPRESS_Q35
     bool
     select PCI_EXPRESS
diff --git a/hw/pci-host/meson.build b/hw/pci-host/meson.build
index 3217e7e..a8c9716 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/meson.build
+++ b/hw/pci-host/meson.build
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PAM', if_true: files('pam.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCI_BONITO', if_true: files('bonito.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_GT64120', if_true: files('gt64120.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCI_EXPRESS_ASPEED', if_true: files('aspeed_pcie.c'))
+pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCI_EXPRESS_BRCMSTB', if_true: files('brcmstb_pcie.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCI_EXPRESS_DESIGNWARE', if_true: files('designware.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCI_EXPRESS_GENERIC_BRIDGE', if_true: files('gpex.c'))
 pci_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_PCI_EXPRESS_GENERIC_BRIDGE', 'CONFIG_ACPI'], if_true: files('gpex-acpi.c'))
diff --git a/hw/pci-host/trace-events b/hw/pci-host/trace-events
index a6fd88c..4fcf818 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/trace-events
+++ b/hw/pci-host/trace-events
@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@ aspeed_pcie_cfg_rw(uint32_t id, const char *dir, uint8_t bus, uint8_t devfn, uin
 aspeed_pcie_phy_read(uint32_t id, uint64_t addr, uint32_t value) "%d: addr 0x%" PRIx64 " value 0x%" PRIx32
 aspeed_pcie_phy_write(uint32_t id, uint64_t addr, uint32_t value) "%d: addr 0x%" PRIx64 " value 0x%" PRIx32
 
+# brcmstb_pcie.c
+brcmstb_pcie_read(uint32_t domain, uint64_t offset, unsigned size, uint64_t value) "pcie%u: [0x%04" PRIx64 "] (%u) -> 0x%08" PRIx64
+brcmstb_pcie_write(uint32_t domain, uint64_t offset, unsigned size, uint64_t value) "pcie%u: [0x%04" PRIx64 "] (%u) <- 0x%08" PRIx64
+brcmstb_pcie_outbound(uint32_t domain, unsigned n, uint64_t cpu, uint64_t pci, uint64_t size) "pcie%u: outbound %u: aperture 0x%" PRIx64 " -> PCI 0x%" PRIx64 ", 0x%" PRIx64 " bytes"
+brcmstb_pcie_inbound(uint32_t domain, unsigned bar, uint64_t pci, uint64_t cpu, uint64_t size) "pcie%u: inbound %u: PCI 0x%" PRIx64 " -> 0x%" PRIx64 ", 0x%" PRIx64 " bytes"
+brcmstb_pcie_perst(uint32_t domain, bool asserted) "pcie%u: PERST# asserted %d"
+brcmstb_pcie_bridge_reset(uint32_t domain) "pcie%u: bridge reset"
+brcmstb_pcie_msi(uint32_t domain, uint32_t vector) "pcie%u: MSI vector %u"
+
 # bonito.c
 bonito_spciconf_small_access(uint64_t addr, unsigned size) "PCI config address is smaller then 32-bit, addr: 0x%"PRIx64", size: %u"
 
